IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oa1-part1-amount`

-- Tests of oa1-part1-amount. Every expected value is worked by hand from the text, with the arithmetic beside it.

§ `s 7(1): the basic amount`

-- Line 155: $273.80 for a month in the payment quarter commencing on January 1, 1985 (January to March 1985).
#ASSERT `s 7(1): the amount of the full monthly pension for a month in the payment quarter commencing on January 1, 1985` EQUALS 273.80
#ASSERT `s 7(1): the amount of the full monthly pension stated for the month` (YMD 1985 1 1) EQUALS JUST 273.80
#ASSERT `s 7(1): the amount of the full monthly pension stated for the month` (YMD 1985 3 31) EQUALS JUST 273.80
-- NOT COVERED: the text states no figure for the quarter before (October to December 1984) nor, in s 7(1), for the quarter after.
#ASSERT `s 7(1): the amount of the full monthly pension stated for the month` (YMD 1984 12 31) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(1): the amount of the full monthly pension stated for the month` (YMD 1985 4 1) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 7(2) to (4): the quarterly adjustment`

-- A quarter must commence after March 31, 1985 (line 157). The quarter that commences on January 1, 1985 is not adjusted.
#ASSERT `s 7(2) to (4): the quarterly adjustment` (YMD 1985 1 1) 273.80 101 100 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(2) to (4): the quarterly adjustment` (YMD 1985 3 31) 273.80 101 100 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- April 1, 1985, indices 101.0 over 100.0, no hold: 273.80 times 101/100 = 27653.80/100 = 276.538. Nothing is carried forward.
#ASSERT `s 7(2) to (4): the quarterly adjustment` (YMD 1985 4 1) 273.80 101 100 NOTHING EQUALS JUST (`s 7(2): Result of a quarterly adjustment` OF 276.538, NOTHING)
-- Equal indices: ratio 1, the amount stands; 7(4)(a) applies only if the first is LOWER than the second.
#ASSERT `s 7(2) to (4): the quarterly adjustment` (YMD 1985 7 1) 273.80 100 100 NOTHING EQUALS JUST (`s 7(2): Result of a quarterly adjustment` OF 273.80, NOTHING)
-- A fall (99.0 against 100.0): no adjustment (7(4)(a)); the second index, 100.0, is carried forward as the base (7(4)(b)).
#ASSERT `s 7(2) to (4): the quarterly adjustment` (YMD 1985 7 1) 273.80 99 100 NOTHING EQUALS JUST (`s 7(2): Result of a quarterly adjustment` OF 273.80, JUST 100)
-- The next quarter, with 100.0 carried: a first index of 99.5, or of 100.0 exactly, is not HIGHER than 100.0: still no adjustment, base kept.
#ASSERT `s 7(2) to (4): the quarterly adjustment` (YMD 1985 10 1) 273.80 99.5 99 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST (`s 7(2): Result of a quarterly adjustment` OF 273.80, JUST 100)
#ASSERT `s 7(2) to (4): the quarterly adjustment` (YMD 1985 10 1) 273.80 100 99 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST (`s 7(2): Result of a quarterly adjustment` OF 273.80, JUST 100)
-- ... and when the first index is higher than the carried base (102.0 over 100.0) the adjustment is made against the BASE, not against the
-- quarter's own second index (here 95.0): 273.80 times 102/100 = 279.276, and the hold ends.
#ASSERT `s 7(2) to (4): the quarterly adjustment` (YMD 1986 1 1) 273.80 102 95 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST (`s 7(2): Result of a quarterly adjustment` OF 279.276, NOTHING)

§ `s 7(5): the increase at 75`

-- Born May 15, 1946: 75 on May 15, 2021. The increase runs "beginning in the payment quarter commencing on July 1, 2022" from the month
-- after the month of the birthday, so it starts in July 2022: 700.00 times 1.10 = 770.00. For June 2022 the amount is 700.00.
#ASSERT `s 7(5): the amount increased by 10% for a person aged 75 or older` (YMD 2022 7 1) (YMD 1946 5 15) 700 EQUALS 770
#ASSERT `s 7(5): the amount increased by 10% for a person aged 75 or older` (YMD 2022 6 15) (YMD 1946 5 15) 700 EQUALS 700
-- Born March 10, 1950: 75 on March 10, 2025. March 2025 (the month in which 75 is attained) is not increased; April 2025 is.
#ASSERT `s 7(5): the amount increased by 10% for a person aged 75 or older` (YMD 2025 3 31) (YMD 1950 3 10) 700 EQUALS 700
#ASSERT `s 7(5): the amount increased by 10% for a person aged 75 or older` (YMD 2025 4 1) (YMD 1950 3 10) 700 EQUALS 770
-- A person who is 74 gets nothing extra (born March 10, 1951, month January 2026).
#ASSERT `s 7(5): the amount increased by 10% for a person aged 75 or older` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 1951 3 10) 700 EQUALS 700

§ `s 3(3) to (5): the partial pension`

-- s 3(4): "rounded to the lower multiple of a year".
#ASSERT `s 3(4): the aggregate period rounded to the lower multiple of a year` 24.9 EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `s 3(4): the aggregate period rounded to the lower multiple of a year` 25 EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `s 3(4): the aggregate period rounded to the lower multiple of a year` 39.99 EQUALS 39
-- s 3(3): 25 whole years: 700 times 25/40 = 437.5. 24.9 years counts as 24: 700 times 24/40 = 420.
#ASSERT `s 3(3): the amount of a partial monthly pension` 700 700 25 EQUALS 437.5
#ASSERT `s 3(3): the amount of a partial monthly pension` 700 700 24.9 EQUALS 420
-- s 2.1(1): the full pension in s 3(3) is the amount before any increase under 7.1(1) or (2): a different "after" amount changes nothing.
#ASSERT `s 3(3): the amount of a partial monthly pension` 700 9999 25 EQUALS 437.5
-- s 3(5): a period beginning on or after the day of approval of a partial pension cannot increase the amount; an earlier one is not barred.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(5): the amount of monthly pension payable may be increased on the basis of the period of residence` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(5): the amount of monthly pension payable may be increased on the basis of the period of residence` TRUE (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2026 10 1))
#ASSERT `s 3(5): the amount of monthly pension payable may be increased on the basis of the period of residence` TRUE (YMD 2026 9 30) (YMD 2026 10 1)
#ASSERT `s 3(5): the amount of monthly pension payable may be increased on the basis of the period of residence` FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2026 10 1)

§ `s 7.1(4): the months that count`

-- Born March 15, 1955 (70 in March 2025). Qualified March 15, 2020; approved March 10, 2021. The period is April 2020 to March 2021: 12 months.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(4): the number of months for which the pension is increased` (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 10) (YMD 1955 3 15) 0 EQUALS 12
-- Two months in which the pension would not have been paid (7.1(4)(c)) leave 10.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(4): the number of months for which the pension is increased` (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 10) (YMD 1955 3 15) 2 EQUALS 10
-- Approved in the month in which the person became qualified: the period is empty.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(4): the number of months for which the pension is increased` (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2020 3 31) (YMD 1955 3 15) 0 EQUALS 0
-- 7.1(4)(a): no month before July 2013. Qualified March 1, 2013, approved June 10, 2014: the period starts in July 2013, not April 2013: July 2013 to June 2014 is 12 months.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(4): the number of months for which the pension is increased` (YMD 2013 3 1) (YMD 2014 6 10) (YMD 1948 3 1) 0 EQUALS 12
-- 7.1(4)(b): no month after the month in which the person attains 70. Born March 10, 1950: qualified at 65 (March 10, 2015), approved January 5, 2021:
-- April 2015 to March 2020 is 60 months, the most there can be.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(4): the number of months for which the pension is increased` (YMD 2015 3 10) (YMD 2021 1 5) (YMD 1950 3 10) 0 EQUALS 60
-- The count never goes below zero: 3 months in the period (April to June 2020), 5 excluded.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(4): the number of months for which the pension is increased` (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2020 6 1) (YMD 1955 3 15) 5 EQUALS 0

§ `s 7.1(1) and (2): the increase for each month`

-- 0.6% of 700.00 is 4.20 a month. 12 months: 700 times 1.072 = 750.40. 60 months: 700 times 1.36 = 952. None: 700.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(1): the amount of the full monthly pension as it is increased` 700 12 EQUALS 750.4
#ASSERT `s 7.1(1): the amount of the full monthly pension as it is increased` 700 60 EQUALS 952
#ASSERT `s 7.1(1): the amount of the full monthly pension as it is increased` 700 0 EQUALS 700
-- Partial: 437.50 times 1.072 = 469.00.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(2): the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is increased` 437.5 12 EQUALS 469

§ `s 7.1(5) and (6): the increase at 75 on the increased amount`

-- Born March 10, 1950; April 2025; 750.40 times 1.10 = 825.44. Partial 469.00 times 1.10 = 515.90. In March 2025, no increase.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(5): the amount of the full monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (1) and increased by 10% at 75` (YMD 2025 4 1) (YMD 1950 3 10) 750.4 EQUALS 825.44
#ASSERT `s 7.1(5): the amount of the full monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (1) and increased by 10% at 75` (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 1950 3 10) 750.4 EQUALS 750.4
#ASSERT `s 7.1(6): the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (2) and increased by 10% at 75` (YMD 2025 4 1) (YMD 1950 3 10) 469 EQUALS 515.9

§ `s 7.1(3): the greatest amount`

-- The greatest of the amounts there are.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(3): the amount of monthly pension the person is to receive` (JUST 750.4) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST 750.4
#ASSERT `s 7.1(3): the amount of monthly pension the person is to receive` NOTHING (JUST 469) (JUST 437.5) FALSE EQUALS JUST 469
#ASSERT `s 7.1(3): the amount of monthly pension the person is to receive` NOTHING (JUST 400) (JUST 437.5) FALSE EQUALS JUST 437.5
#ASSERT `s 7.1(3): the amount of monthly pension the person is to receive` (JUST 500) (JUST 469) (JUST 437.5) FALSE EQUALS JUST 500
-- NOT COVERED: "unless they decide otherwise" (the Act does not say what the person then receives), and no amount at all.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(3): the amount of monthly pension the person is to receive` (JUST 500) (JUST 469) (JUST 437.5) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7.1(3): the amount of monthly pension the person is to receive` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
